        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Determine ask oracle agent",
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776970643937"
          },
          "code": "DETERMINE_ASK_ORACLE_AGENT",
          "id": "1776970477520",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776970477521_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a scope-classification agent for Conformance Check questions.\n\n## CONFORMANCE CHECK BASICS\n\nConformance check evaluates whether a batch meets expected parameter limits.\n\nEach batch has a primary product. The primary product can have one or more conformance parameters.\n\nFor each conformance parameter, the system calculates a parameter value using:\n- ingredient actual values\n- ingredient quantities\n- batch quantity\n- UOM conversions\n\nIf an ingredient is missing an actual value, that ingredient actual value is treated as 0 for the calculation.\n\nThe calculated value is compared against the parameter's expected limits:\n- `MinimumTargetValue`: the minimum acceptable value\n- `MaximumTargetValue`: the maximum acceptable value\n- `TargetValue`: the ideal or best-result milestone value; it is not itself the pass/fail limit\n\nPossible conformance statuses:\n- `In range`: the calculated value is between the minimum and maximum value\n- `Out of range`: the calculated value is below or above the minimum and maximum value\n- `Incomplete`: the system could not fully evaluate the conformance result, or required data/errors indicate the result is incomplete\n\n## Main Task\n\nYour task is to classify the user's question as exactly one of these four values:\n\n- `plant` = the question is about multiple batches, work orders, products, or plant-wide conformance activity, and simple sort based on direct attributes, but does not require aggregation, calculated metrics, comparisons, counts, percentages, or totals.\n- `plant_metric` = the question is about cross-batch analysis that requires aggregation, summarization, grouping, comparison, calculated or rolled-up sorting, counts, percentages, totals, or highest/lowest values across batches, work orders, or products.\n- `batch` = the question is about one specific batch, work order, or a single work-order-specific result\n- `unrelated` = the question is not related to conformance check\n\nCurrent user question:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nChat history:\n {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} \n\nReturn exactly one valid JSON object and nothing else, using one of these four forms:\n\n{\n  \"scope\": \"plant\"\n}\n\n{\n  \"scope\": \"plant_metric\"\n}\n\n{\n  \"scope\": \"batch\"\n}\n\n{\n  \"scope\": \"unrelated\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- Return only valid JSON\n- Do not include markdown\n- Do not include explanations\n- Do not include extra fields\n- The `scope` value must be exactly `plant`,`plant_metric`,`batch` or `unrelated`\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nHOW TO USE CHAT HISTORY\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nUse chat history only to resolve whether the current message refers to a previously established batch/work order.\n\nYou may use chat history to resolve:\n- \"this batch\"\n- \"that work order\"\n- \"the same batch\"\n- \"it\"\n- omitted follow-up references such as:\n  - \"Why is it incomplete?\"\n  - \"Show me the ingredients\"\n  - \"Run it now\"\n  - \"What are the results?\"\n\nPrecedence rules:\n1. If the current user message explicitly mentions a batch/work order, use that and ignore prior batch references\n2. If the current user message does not explicitly mention a batch/work order, use chat history only if it clearly refers to one previously established batch/work order\n3. If the current user message is clearly about one previously established batch/work order, classify as `batch`\n4. If the current user message is about multiple batches or plant-wide analysis, classify as `plant` or `plant_metric`\n5. If unsure, prefer the most specific interpretation clearly supported by the current message and chat history\n\nImportant:\n- Do not let chat history override an explicit batch/work order in the current message\n- Do not invent a batch/work order that does not appear in the current message or chat history\n- Use chat history only for scope resolution, not for answering anything else\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nDECISION RULES\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nChoose `batch` when the question is about one specific batch or work order.\n\nThis includes cases where the user:\n- names a specific batch or work order\n- says `this batch`\n- says `this work order`\n- says `that batch`\n- says `that work order`\n- asks about ingredients, parameters, errors, simulations, or conformance results for one batch\n- asks a follow-up question that clearly refers to one previously established batch\n- asks about specific items/lots \n- asks about specific conformance parameter actual values in the system \n\n- Important:\n  If the user asks about a specific batch or work order, classify as `batch` even if the question mentions product, ingredient, lot, target value, or actual value.\n\nChoose `plant` when the question is about plant-level or multi-batch conformance records that do not require calculated metrics.\n\nThis includes cases where the user asks about:\n- all batches\n- multiple batches\n- lists or filters of batches / work orders / products\n- products across batches when only listing or filtering is needed\n- plant-wide conformance risk when the user asks for matching records\n- simple sort based on direct attributes\n- product specification targets\n- ingredient, ingredient-lot actual values cross-batch\n- available ingredients based on direct value filters\n- target values for a specific product (and conformance parameter)\n- actual values for an ingredient or ingredient lot (and conformance parameter)\n- other general conformance check questions\n\n- Ingredient override:\n  Choose `plant`for cross-batch ingredient-related questions, even if the question also asks for aggregation, counts, percentages, rankings, top/bottom, highest/lowest, grouping, summaries, comparisons, or trends.\n  Do not classify ingredient-related questions as `plant_metric`.\n\nChoose `plant_metric` when the question is about cross-batch analysis that requires calculated metrics.\n\nThis includes cases where the user asks about:\n- trends\n- counts\n- percentages\n- calculated or rolled-up sorting/ranking\n- highest/lowest values\n- batches by severity\n- products across batches when comparison, grouping, or summarization is needed\n- parameters across batches\n- cross-batch summaries\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nINTERPRETATION RULES\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n- `Batch`, `Work Order`, and `WorkOrderNumber` mean the same thing\n- If the question is about a single named or implied batch, return `batch`\n- Follow-up questions that continue discussing one previously established batch should be classified as `batch`\n- If unsure, prefer the most specific interpretation supported by the conversation\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nEXAMPLES\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nExamples without chat history:\n- \"Show me all unreleased batches with conformance risks\" -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n- \"Which parameter is most frequently out of range?\" -> {\"scope\":\"plant_metric\"}\n- \"Give me conformance results for batch Berry Foods\" -> {\"scope\":\"batch\"}\n- \"Why is this batch incomplete?\" -> {\"scope\":\"batch\"}\n- \"Which ingredients in work order Berry Foods are contributing to the issue?\" -> {\"scope\":\"batch\"}\n- \"Show me the top 10 batches with conformance issues\" -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n- \"Run conformance check for batch Berry Foods\" -> {\"scope\":\"batch\"}\n- Which batches are currently out of range for parameter {potency}? -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n- Which unreleased batches have calculated values deviating by more than 100% from the target value for {potency}? -> {\"scope\":\"plant_metric\"}\n- Sort conformance-issue batches by planned date (earliest first). -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n- Sort conformance-issue batches by number of parameters at risk. -> {\"scope\":\"plant_metric\"}\n- Which conformance-issue batches have missing conformance parameter values of ingredients? -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n- Show me key ingredients without conformance values that are contributing to conformance issues in batches. (key = equal to or more than 10 out-of-range batches) -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n- Show me the trend of conformance-issue batch count over the last 7 days. -> {\"scope\":\"plant_metric\"}\n- Which product has the highest % of conformance-risk unreleased batches? -> {\"scope\":\"plant_metric\"}\n- Show me reserved ingredients that have low (or high) conformance parameter values. -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n- Show me all available ingredient lots that have low (or high) conformance parameter values. -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n- What are the target values for product X for conformance parameter CP1. -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n- Show me the actual values for ingredient A (or ingredient A-lot X) for conformance parameter CP1. -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}\n\nExamples using chat history:\n- Previous turn established batch `Berry Foods`; current question: \"Why is it incomplete?\" -> {\"scope\":\"batch\"}\n- Previous turn established batch `Berry Foods`; current question: \"Show me the ingredients\" -> {\"scope\":\"batch\"}\n- Previous turn established batch `Berry Foods`; current question: \"Run it now\" -> {\"scope\":\"batch\"}\n- Previous turn established batch `Berry Foods`; current question: \"Which batches are currently out of range?\" -> {\"scope\":\"plant\"}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\"scope\":\"\"},\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create conformance results summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_CONFORMANCE_RESULTS_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1775066235434",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775066235437_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Analyze the data object from {{$context.$nodes.GET_SUMMARY_CONFORMANCE_RESULTS.$output}} and generate a clear, single-paragraph 30-word production update that reads like a brief for senior leadership.\n\nThe data represents the status of batches in respect to conformance check.\n\n**IMPORTANT**\nDo not mention any IDs (like organization ids, work order is or any of that)"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "With the following JSON: {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRIORITY_NOT_ATTEMPTED_BATCHES.$output}} \n\nFor each item in the list:\n\n1. Generate `ora.Agent(\"<WorkOrderId>\")`, where `<WorkOrderId>` is the value of the `WorkOrderId` field for that row if the `ConformanceCheckResultStatus` is \"NOT_ATTEMPTED\"\n2. Set the following properties:\n\n   * **shortDescription** → \"Run conformance check - the batch is scheduled for <PlannedStartDate>\" where <PleannedStartDate> is the value of the `PlannedStartDate` field for that row\n   * **title** → Based on the \"Conformance check for batch <WorkOrderNumber>\"  where <WorkOrderNumber> is the value of the `WorkOrderNumber` field for that row\n   * ** priority** → true\n   * **actionText** → \"Run Check\"\n\n**IMPORTANT\n**PlannedStartDate should be formatted in MM/DD/YYYY"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display priority actions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_PRIORITY_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1774895427710",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774895427713_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "With the following JSON: {{$context.$nodes.GET_PRIORITY_NOT_ATTEMPTED_BATCHES.$output}} \n\nFor each item in the list:\n\nExtract 'WorkOrderId' , 'WorkOrderNumber','PlannedStartDate'  to generate the following action:\n\n1. Generate `ora.Invoke(refreshAgent,{\"command\": \"RunCheck\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<WorkOrderNumber>})` , where `<WorkOrderId>` and <WorkOrderNumber> are the values of the `WorkOrderId`and `WorkOrderNumber` fields for that row\n2. Set the following properties:\n\n   * **shortDescription** → \"The batch is scheduled for <PlannedStartDate>\" where <PleannedStartDate> is the value of the `PlannedStartDate` field for that row\n   * **title** → Based on the \"Conformance check for batch <WorkOrderNumber>\"  where <WorkOrderNumber> is the value of the `WorkOrderNumber` field for that row\n   * ** priority** → true\n   * **actionText** → \"Run Check\"\n\n**IMPORTANT\n**PlannedStartDate should be formatted in MM/DD/YYYY\n\nFor the shortDescription of the action, use the extracted `PlannedStartDate` value and compare it against:\n\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nApply the rules below exactly as written.\n\nImportant rules:\n- `PlannedStartDate` is in `YYYY-MM-DD` format\n- Compare dates only at the calendar-day level\n- Ignore all time components\n- Determine the difference in whole days between `PlannedStartDate` and `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`\n\nOutput rules for the short description:\n\n1. If `PlannedStartDate` is the same calendar date as `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display text: `Due today`\n   - Display a badge with priority: `Warning`\n\n2. If `PlannedStartDate` is exactly 1 day after `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display text: `Due tomorrow`\n   - Display a badge with priority: `Medium`\n\n3. If `PlannedStartDate` is before `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display text: `<N> days past due`\n   - Replace `<N>` with the absolute number of days between the two dates\n   - Display a badge with priority: `Alert`\n\n4. If `PlannedStartDate` is more than 1 day after `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display the `StartDate` formatted as `MM/DD/YYYY`\n   - Display a badge with priority: `Medium`\n\n   Do not use any other wording.\n   Do not include time values.\n   Do not infer hours or partial days.\n   Use only one of the four outputs above."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is ora form submission"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1775583561381",
            "false": "1774631380582"
          },
          "code": "IS_ORA_FORM_SUBMISSION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1775071761331",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775071761335_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.DETERMINE_IF_IS_ORA_FORM_SUBMISSION.$output.result.FormId != null}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create email data object",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "let records = $context.$nodes.GET_INCOMPLETE_RESULTS_FOR_NOTIFY.$output.items;\n\nlet jsonArr = [];\n\nrecords.forEach(record =>{\n\n        let errorMsg = \"\";\n\n       let recordErrors = record.ConformanceCheckResultErrors.items;\n       if(recordErrors.length>0){\n           let errorCount = recordErrors[0].ErrorCount;\n\n           if(errorCount>1){\n               errorMsg = \"Multiple issues\";\n           }else{\n               let errorCode = recordErrors[0].ErrorCode;\n               let errorMessage = recordErrors[0].MessageText;\n               let errorTokenNames = recordErrors[0].ErrorTokenNames;\n               let errorTokenValues = recordErrors[0].ErrorTokenValues;\n\n               if(errorCode === \"WIE_INGRDNT_QTY_NOT_RESERVED\" || errorCode===\"WIE_ASSIGNMENT_NOT_FOUND\"){\n                    errorMsg = errorMessage.replace(`{${errorTokenNames}}`,errorTokenValues);\n\n              }else if(errorCode===\"WIE_TARGET_VALUE_MISSING\" || errorCode===\"WIE_UOM_CONVERSION_MISSING\"){\n                   let names = errorTokenNames.split(\",\");\n                   let values = errorTokenValues .split(\",\");\n\n                   let map = {};\n                   names.forEach((name, i) => {\n                        map[name.trim()] = values[i]?.trim();\n                   });\n\n                   errorMsg= errorMessage.replace(/\\{(.*?)\\}/g, (_, token) => {\n                       return map[token] || `{${token}}`;\n                     });\n\n              }\n           } \n       }else{\n           errorMsg = \"Incomplete\";\n       }\n         \n        let obj = {\n             \"BatchName\":record.WorkOrderNumber,\n             \"BatchQuantity\":record.BatchQuantity,\n             \"Item\":record.ItemNumber,\n             \"StartDate\":record.PlannedStartDate.split(\"T\")[0],\n             \"Error\": errorMsg\n        };\n\n        jsonArr.push(obj);\n\n\n});\n\n\nreturn jsonArr;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774987229238"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_EMAIL_DATA_OBJECT",
          "id": "1776099607859",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
