          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_CONFORMANCE_CHECK_RESULTS",
          "id": "1774371686070",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774371686072_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following Array of Json objects to generate a single multiRecordWidget : {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_CONFORMANCE_CHECK_RECORDS.$output.result}} \n\nThe columns for the multiRecordWidget should be \"Batch\",\"Primary Product\",\"Start Date\",\"Conformance Result\",\"Batch Quantity\"\n\n1) Extract `Batch`, `PrimaryProduct`,`StartDate`, `BatchQuantity` , `BatchUomCode` ,`ConformanceResult`,`WorkOrderId` from each item in the array to populate each row in multiRecordWidget \n\n**Important:**\n-For the \"Batch quantity\" column display both the BatchQuantity and BatchUomCode\n-For the \"Conformance Result\" column:\n   -Evaluate the value of \"Conformance Result\" and display a badge based on the following mapping:\n   -\"OUT_OF_RANGE\" → alert\n   -\"NOT_ATTEMPTED\" → medium\n   -\"INCOMPLETE\" → warning\n\n\n* #ACTION For each row, If the value of ConformanceResult is \"NOT_ATTEMPTED\" or \"INCOMPLETE\", generate an actionable insight using the following options:\ntitle:\"RunCheck\"\nfollowUpCommand: ora.Invoke(refreshAgent,{\"command\": \"RunCheck\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>})   where <WorkOrderId> and <Batch> are the values you extracted from the array\nactionText: \"Run Check\"\nshortDescription: \"Executes the conformance check for the specificed batch\"\nrefreshAgents :true\n\n* If instead the value of ConformanceResult is \"OUT_OF_RANGE\" , generate an actionable insight using the following options:\ntitle:\"ViewResults\"\nfollowUpCommand: ora.Agent({\"command\": \"ViewDetails\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>})   where <WorkOrderId> ,<Batch> are the values you extracted from the array\nactionText: \"View Results\"\nshortDescription: \"View the conformance check result details of the specified batch.\"\n\n**IMPORTANT\n-The title should be: \"Scheduled batches with highest conformance risk\"\n-Generate a brief summary explaining that conformance issues highlight batches where quality is drifting from expected standards.Invite the user to Review the highest-impact issues first to understand potential quality or compliance risk, then take corrective action before they affect downstream production to reduce wastage or rework.\n\nFor the `Start Date` column, use the extracted `StartDate` value and compare it against:\n\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nApply the rules below exactly as written.\n\nImportant rules:\n\n-If the data is empty, do not mention the JSON or say that no data was found in the JSON.\n\nInstead, display a user-facing message where you explain that There are currently no batches identified with conformance check results in the specified time frame.\n\nRules for empty data message:\n- Use this exact meaning in the response\n- Keep the message user-friendly and concise\n- Do not mention internal implementation details such as JSON, payload, dataset, or response structure\n- Do not say \"there is no data in the JSON\"\n- If the data is empty, show only the empty-state message\n\n- `StartDate` is in `YYYY-MM-DD` format\n- Compare dates only at the calendar-day level\n- Ignore all time components\n- Determine the difference in whole days between `StartDate` and `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`\n\nOutput rules for the `Start Date` column:\n\n1. If `StartDate` is the same calendar date as `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display text: `Due today`\n\n2. If `StartDate` is exactly 1 day after `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display text: `Due tomorrow`\n\n3. If `StartDate` is before `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display text: `<N> days past due`\n   - Replace `<N>` with the absolute number of days between the two dates\n\n4. If `StartDate` is more than 1 day after `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display the `StartDate` formatted as `MM/DD/YYYY`\n\n   Do not use any other wording.\n   Do not include time values.\n   Do not infer hours or partial days.\n   Use only one of the four outputs above."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
