          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display out of range results"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_OUT_OF_RANGE_RESULTS",
          "id": "1774379635807",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774379635809_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use this array of JSON objects to generate exactly one `multiRecordWidget` when data exists:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_OUT_OF_RANGE_LIST.$output.result}}\n\nIf there is no data in the json array, follow the EMPTY STATE REQUIREMENT below.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nEMPTY STATE REQUIREMENT\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore generating any widget, first determine whether the array contains at least one item.\n\nIf the array is empty, null, missing, or contains no displayable rows:\n\n- Do not generate a `multiRecordWidget`\n- Do not generate any table, list, or fallback widget\n- Do not display the summary\n- Display only this exact user-facing message:\n\nThere are currently no batches with out-of-range results in the specified time frame.\n\nThis empty-state message is the complete response when there is no data.\n\nDo not mention JSON, payloads, datasets, or internal implementation details.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nWIDGET REQUIREMENTS\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nGenerate exactly one `multiRecordWidget`.\n\nThe widget must have these columns:\n- `Batch`\n- `Primary Product`\n- `Batch Quantity`\n- `Start Date`\n- `Check Date`\n\nFrom each item in the array, extract these fields:\n- `Batch`\n- `PrimaryProduct`\n- `BatchQuantity`\n- `BatchUomCode`\n- `StartDate`\n- `ConformanceCheckResultDate`\n- `WorkOrderId` (used only for actions, not displayed)\n\nDo not omit any rows.\nEvery item in the array must appear in the widget.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nCOLUMN MAPPING\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nPopulate each row as follows:\n\n- `Batch` = `Batch`\n- `Primary Product` = `PrimaryProduct`\n- `Batch Quantity` = display `BatchQuantity` together with `BatchUomCode`\n- `Start Date` = formatted according to the rules below\n- `Check Date` = `ConformanceCheckResultDate` formatted as `MM/DD/YYYY HH:MM`\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nROW ACTION\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nEvery row must include this action:\n\n- `title`: `ViewResults`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\":\"ViewDetails\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>})`\n- `actionText`: `View Results`\n- `shortDescription`: `View the conformance check result details of the specified batch.`\n\nUse the `WorkOrderId` and `Batch` values from that same row.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nSUMMARY\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nAbove the widget, display a brief summary that explains what out-of-range status means.\n\nThe summary should explain that out-of-range batches are batches where quality is drifting from expected standards based on the conformance parameter setup.\n\nThe summary should also encourage the user to review and take corrective action before the issue affects downstream production, increases wastage, or causes rework.\n\nKeep the summary concise and user-friendly.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTART DATE FORMAT RULES\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFor the `Start Date` column, use the extracted `StartDate` value and compare it against:\n\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nImportant rules:\n- `StartDate` is in `YYYY-MM-DD` format\n- Compare dates only at the calendar-day level\n- Ignore all time components\n- Determine the whole-day difference between `StartDate` and `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`\n\nUse exactly one of these outputs:\n\n1. If `StartDate` is the same calendar date as `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - display text: `Due today`\n\n2. If `StartDate` is exactly 1 day after `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - display text: `Due tomorrow`\n\n3. If `StartDate` is before `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - display text: `<N> days past due`\n   - replace `<N>` with the absolute whole-day difference\n\n4. If `StartDate` is more than 1 day after `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - display the date formatted as `MM/DD/YYYY`\n\nDo not use any other wording.\nDo not include time values.\nDo not infer hours or partial days.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nIMPORTANT RULES\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n- First check the EMPTY STATE REQUIREMENT before generating any output\n- Generate exactly one `multiRecordWidget` when data exists\n- Show only the empty-state message when the array is empty, null, missing, or contains no displayable rows\n- Do not omit any rows\n- Do not mention JSON or internal processing details\n- Use the action on every row\n- Format `Check Date` as `MM/DD/YYYY HH:MM`\n- Format `Batch Quantity` using both `BatchQuantity` and `BatchUomCode`"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display incomplete results"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_INCOMPLETE_RESULTS",
          "id": "1774380204632",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774380204633_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following Array of Json objects to generate a single multiRecordWidget : {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_INCOMPLETE_RESULTS_RECORDS.$output.result}}\n\nThe columns for the multiRecordWidget should be \"Batch\",\"Primary Product\",\"Batch Quantity\",\"Start Date\",\"Check Date\" and \"Reason\"\n\n1) Extract `Batch`, `PrimaryProduct`,`BatchQuantity`, `BatchUomCode`,`StartDate` ,`ConformanceCheckResultDate` and `Reason` from each item in the array to populate each row in multiRecordWidget \n**Also extract `WorkOrderId` (this will not be shown but will be used below)\n\n* #ACTION For each row, generate an actionable insight using the following options:\ntitle:\"ViewErrors\"\nfollowUpCommand: ora.Agent({\"command\": \"ViewErrors\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>})   where <WorkOrderId> and <Batch> are the values you extracted from the array\nactionText: \"View Errors\"\nshortDescription: \"View the conformance check errors for the specified batch.\"\n\n**IMPORTANT\n-For the \"Batch quantity\" column display both the `BatchQuantity` and `BatchUomCode`\n-If the value for <Reason> is null, display \"Incomplete\"\n-The title should be: \"Incomplete conformance results\"\n-Generate a brief summary explaining what out of range status means(  meaning that an error happened during conformance check like uom conversion errors, ingredients not being reserved,invalid conformance setup) .Invite the user to take corrective action before they affect downstream production to reduce wastage or rework.\nFor the `Start Date` column, use the extracted `StartDate` value and compare it against:\n\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nApply the rules below exactly as written.\n\nImportant rules:\n\n-If the JSON array does not contain data for you to generate the widget, do not generate it, instead, display this user-facing message:\n\nThere are currently no batches with incomplete results in the specified time frame.\n\nRules for empty data message:\n- Use this exact meaning in the response\n- Keep the message user-friendly and concise\n- Do not mention internal implementation details such as JSON, payload, dataset, or response structure\n- Do not say \"there is no data in the JSON\"\n- If the data is empty, show only the empty-state message\n\n- `StartDate` is in `YYYY-MM-DD` format\n- Compare dates only at the calendar-day level\n- Ignore all time components\n- Determine the difference in whole days between `StartDate` and `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`\n\nOutput rules for the `Start Date` column:\n\n1. If `StartDate` is the same calendar date as `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display text: `Due today`\n\n2. If `StartDate` is exactly 1 day after `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display text: `Due tomorrow`\n\n3. If `StartDate` is before `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display text: `<N> days past due`\n   - Replace `<N>` with the absolute number of days between the two dates\n\n4. If `StartDate` is more than 1 day after `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`:\n   - Display the `StartDate` formatted as `MM/DD/YYYY`\n\nDo not use any other wording.\nDo not include time values.\nDo not infer hours or partial days.\nUse only one of the four outputs above.\n-For the \"Check Date\" column:\n*Display the `ConformanceCheckResultDate` in MM/DD/YYYY formart, do not display any time components from the date."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
