          "id": "1775583638585",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775583638586_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following array of  Json objects to generate a single multiRecordWidget : {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_BASIC_SIMULATION_RESULTS.$output.result}} \n\nThe columns for the multiRecordWidget should be \"Conformance Parameter\",\"Minimum Value\",\"Maximum Value\",\"Target Value\",\"Calculated Value\" and \"Conformance Result\"\n\n1) Extract `ParameterCode`, `MinimumTargetValue`,`MaximumTargetValue`,`TargetValue`,`CalculatedValue`,`ConformanceCheckResultStatus`  from each JSON inside the array to populate the rows in the multiRecordWidget \n**Also extract `WorkOrderNumber`\n\nDisplay a header saying 'Conformance check simulation results' and also display a brief summary about the conformance check simulation  results for the work order <WorkOrderNumber> (use the value you extracted) , you should mention the date (MM/DD/YYYY) on which the conformance check was executed, the status of the conformance check, the summary should provide useful information to the user. Emphasize that these results are for simulation only and that if user still needs to do changes on the batch.\n\n**IMPORTANT\n**Do not mention the WorkOrderId, only WorkOrderNumber/Batch\n**If the status is either \"INCOMPLETE\" or \"OUT_OF_RANGE\" you should give a hint to the user of trying different items for the simulation, reviewing the conformance parameter setup, the actual values and the ingredients of the batch."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
