            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_QUANTITY_SIMULATION_RESULTS",
          "id": "1775608160546",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775608160547_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following array of Json objects to generate a single multiRecordWidget : {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_QUANTITY_SIMULATION_RESULTS.$output.result}} \n\nThe columns for the multiRecordWidget should be \"Conformance Parameter\",\"Minimum Value\",\"Maximum Value\",\"Target Value\",\"Calculated Value\" and \"Conformance Result\"\n\n1) Extract `ParameterCode`, `MinimumTargetValue`,`MaximumTargetValue`,`TargetValue`,`CalculatedValue`,`ConformanceCheckResultStatus`  from each JSON inside the array to populate the rows in the multiRecordWidget \n**Also extract `WorkOrderNumber`\n\nDisplay a header saying 'Conformance check simulation results' and also display a brief summary about the conformance check simulation  results for the work order <WorkOrderNumber> (use the value you extracted) , you should mention the date (MM/DD/YYYY) on which the conformance check was executed, the status of the conformance check, the summary should provide useful information to the user. Emphasize that these results are for simulation only and that if user still needs to do changes on the batch.\n\n**IMPORTANT\n**Do not mention the WorkOrderId, only WorkOrderNumber/Batch\n**If the status is either \"INCOMPLETE\" or \"OUT_OF_RANGE\" you should give a hint to the user of reviewing the conformance parameter setup, the actual values and the ingredients of the batch."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract run check view ingredients payload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let parent = $context.$nodes.GET_CONFORMANCE_CHECK_RESULTS_DETAILS.$output.items;\n\nlet checkDetails = $context.$nodes.GET_CONFORMANCE_CHECK_RESULTS_DETAILS.$output.items[0].ConformanceCheckDetails.items;\n\nlet parentHashRaw = parent[0][\"@context\"].links[0].href.split(\"/\");\n\nlet parentHash = parentHashRaw[parentHashRaw.length-1];\n\n\nlet conformanceCheckViewDetails= checkDetails.map(item => ({\n  \"WorkOrderId\":item.WorkOrderId,\n  \"PrimaryProduct\":item.ItemNumber,\n  \"BatchQuantity\":item.BatchQuantity,\n  \"UomCode\":item.UOMCode,\n  \"UOMCodeConformanceParameter\": item.UOMConformanceParameter,\n  \"QuantityConformanceParameter\":item.QuantityConformanceParameter,\n  \"Batch\":item.WorkOrderNumber,\n  \"ParameterCode\": item.ParameterCode,\n  \"MinimumTargetValue\": item.MinimumTargetValue,\n  \"MaximumTargetValue\": item.MaximumTargetValue,\n  \"TargetValue\":item.TargetValue,\n  \"CalculatedValue\":item.CalculatedValue,\n  \"ConformanceCheckResultStatus\":item.ConformanceCheckResultStatusMeaning,\n  \"ConformanceCheckDate\":item.ConformanceCheckResultDate,\n  \"OverallStatus\":parent[0].ConformanceCheckResult,\n  \"ParentHash\":parentHash,\n  \"DetailId\":item.ConformanceCheckDetailId\n}));\n\nreturn conformanceCheckViewDetails;\n\n"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774472357760"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_RUN_CHECK_VIEW_INGREDIENTS_PAYLOAD",
          "id": "1775591376354",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Display the 4 extra actions below the MultiRecordWidget"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display conformance check details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_CONFORMANCE_CHECK_DETAILS_",
          "id": "1774644272648",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774644272650_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following JSON object array to generate one `multiRecordWidget`:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_VIEW_DETAILS_OBJECT_ARRAY.$output.result}}\n\nGenerate a conformance check results summary and a `multiRecordWidget` using the rules below.\n\nData to extract from each JSON object:\n- ParameterCode\n- CalculatedValue\n- MinimumTargetValue\n- MaximumTargetValue\n- TargetValue\n- ConformanceCheckResultStatus\n- ParentHash\n- DetailId\n- WorkOrderId\n- Batch\n- BatchQuantity\n- UOMCode\n- OverallStatus\n- ConformanceParameterQuantity\n- UOMCodeConformanceParameter\n- ConformanceCheckDate\n- PrimaryProduct\n\nDo not display `WorkOrderId` to the user. Use only the batch/work order number where user-facing text is needed.\n\nHeader rules:\nBuild the widget header using:\n- PrimaryProduct\n- BatchQuantity\n- UOMCode\n- OverallStatus\n\nUse exactly one of the following header formats:\n\nIf `OverallStatus` = `IN_RANGE`:\n`<PrimaryProduct> (<BatchQuantity> <UOMCode>) is in conformance`\n\nIf `OverallStatus` = `OUT_OF_RANGE`:\n`<PrimaryProduct> (<BatchQuantity> <UOMCode>) is out of conformance`\n\nIf `OverallStatus` = `INCOMPLETE`:\n`<PrimaryProduct> (<BatchQuantity> <UOMCode>) has incomplete results`\n\nHeader requirements:\n- Use the extracted values exactly as provided.\n- Do not change the wording.\n- Do not add extra punctuation.\n- Do not add any text before or after the header.\n- Use only one of the three header formats above.\n\nSummary:\nDisplay a brief, useful summary of the conformance check results for batch:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_VIEW_DETAILS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.Batch}}\n\nThe summary must:\n- Mention the batch number.\n- Mention the conformance check execution date using `ConformanceCheckDate`.\n- Format the date as `MM/DD/YYYY`.\n- Mention the overall conformance status.\n- Provide useful context for the user.\n\nIf `OverallStatus` is `INCOMPLETE` or `OUT_OF_RANGE`, include a helpful hint recommending that the user review:\n- the conformance parameter setup,\n- the actual calculated values,\n- and the batch ingredients.\n\nmultiRecordWidget columns:\nCreate the widget with the following columns, in this exact order:\n\n1. Conformance Parameter\n2. Calculated Value\n3. Minimum Value\n4. Maximum Value\n5. Target Value\n6. Conformance Result\n\nMap each row as follows:\n- `Conformance Parameter` = `ParameterCode`\n- `Calculated Value` = `CalculatedValue`\n- `Minimum Value` = `MinimumTargetValue`\n- `Maximum Value` = `MaximumTargetValue`\n- `Target Value` = `TargetValue`\n- `Conformance Result` = `ConformanceCheckResultStatus` (display a badge with the priority depending on the status , if IN RANGE = \"success\" , if OUT OF RANGE = \"alert\")\n\nRow-level action:\nFor each row in the `multiRecordWidget`, add its own action:\n\ntitle: `ViewIngredients`\nfollowUpCommand:\nora.Agent({\n  \"command\": \"ViewIngredients\",\n  \"HashId\": <ParentHash>,\n  \"DetailId\": <DetailId>,\n  \"ParameterCode\": <ParameterCode>,\n  \"ProductQuantity\": <ConformanceParameterQuantity>,\n  \"UomCode\": <UOMCodeConformanceParameter>\n})\nactionText: `View Ingredients`\nshortDescription: `View the batch ingredients`\n\nUse the values from the same JSON object as the row.\n\nExtra actions below the multiRecordWidget:\nDisplay the following actions below the `multiRecordWidget`.\n\nAction 1:\nDisplay this action only when `OverallStatus` = `OUT_OF_RANGE`.\ntitle: `View Recommendations`\nfollowUpCommand:\nora.Agent({\n  \"command\": \"ViewRecommendation\",\n  \"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\n  \"Batch\": <Batch>\n})\nactionText: `View Recommendations`\nshortDescription: `View the recommended ingredients to fix conformance issues`\n\nAction 2:\ntitle: `Recalculate for alternate ingredient lots`\nfollowUpCommand:\nora.Agent({\n  \"command\": \"SimulateLots\",\n  \"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\n  \"Batch\": <Batch>\n})\nactionText: `Recalculate for alternate ingredient lots`\nshortDescription: `Simulate conformance check with substitute lots`\n\nAction 3:\ntitle: `Recalculate for substitute ingredient`\nfollowUpCommand:\nora.Agent({\n  \"command\": \"SimulateIngredients\",\n  \"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\n  \"Batch\": <Batch>,\n  \"HashId\": <ParentHash>,\n  \"DetailId\": <DetailId>\n})\nactionText: `Recalculate for substitute ingredient`\nshortDescription: `Simulate conformance check with substitute ingredients`\n\nAction 4:\ntitle: `Recalculate for adjusted quantities`\nfollowUpCommand:\nora.Agent({\n  \"command\": \"SimulateQuantities\",\n  \"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\n  \"Batch\": <Batch>\n})\nactionText: `Recalculate for adjusted quantities`\nshortDescription: `Simulate conformance check with substitute quantities`\n\nAction 5:\ntitle: `Hold batch`\nfollowUpCommand:\nora.Invoke(refreshAgent, {\n  \"command\": \"HoldBatch\",\n  \"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\n  \"Batch\": <Batch>\n})\nactionText: `Hold batch`\nshortDescription: `Holds the specified batch`\n\nImportant rules:\n- Do not mention or display `WorkOrderId` in any user-facing text.\n- Each row must include its own `View Ingredients` action.\n- The row-level `View Ingredients` action must use values from that same row.\n- The extra actions should use the extracted batch-level values.\n- Display all 5 extra actions mentioned\n- `View Recommendations` should be displayed only when `OverallStatus` is `OUT_OF_RANGE`.\n- If multiple JSON objects contain the same batch-level values, use the values from the first object.\n- Do not invent values. If a required value is missing, leave it blank or omit only that unavailable value from the command payload.\n- Remember to show the badges in the Conformance Result column inside the widget"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Use the following Array of  Json objects to generate a single multiRecordWidget : {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_VIEW_INGR_DETAILS_ARRAY.$output.result}} \n\nThe columns for the multiRecordWidget should be \"Ingredient\",\"Lot\",\"Quantity\",\"ActualValue\"\n\n1) Extract `ItemNumber`, `LotNumber`,`Quantity`,`ActualValue`  from the each json object in the array to populate the rows in the multiRecordWidget \n*Also extract `UOMCode` and `ParameterCode` \n\nI want you to display a brief summary of the conformance check ingredients, you must mention that these ingredients belong to the details for the conformance parameter name : `ParameterCode` \n\n**IMPORTANT\n**For the Quantity column,display both the `Quantity` and `UOMCode` together\n**Display the brief summary above the widget"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display view ingredients"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_VIEW_INGREDIENTS",
          "id": "1774910021899",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774910021901_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following Array of  Json objects to generate a single multiRecordWidget : {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_VIEW_INGR_DETAILS_ARRAY.$output.result}} \n\nThe columns for the multiRecordWidget should be \"Ingredient\",\"Lot\",\"Quantity\",\"Actual Value\",\"Contribution\"\n\n1) Extract `ItemNumber`, `LotNumber`,`Quantity`,`ActualValue`,`Contribution`  from the each json object in the array to populate the rows in the multiRecordWidget \n*Also extract `UOMCode` and `ParameterCode`\n\nDisplay the header:\n\nConformance check ingredients (`ParameterCode`)\n\nBelow the header, write a brief, user-friendly summary explaining how the conformance parameter value is calculated.\n\nThe summary must explain that:\n- each ingredient has an `ActualValue`\n- each ingredient’s `ActualValue` is multiplied by its quantity\n- the sum of those values is used to calculate the final value for the conformance parameter\n\nAlso include these values in the summary:\n- Primary product quantity: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_VIEW_INGREDIENTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.ProductQuantity}}\n- Conformance parameter UOM: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_VIEW_INGREDIENTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.UomCode}}\n\nThe summary must also clearly explain that:\n- the primary product quantity has been converted using the UOM of the conformance parameter\n- this conversion is used so the calculation is performed in the same unit of measure\n\nRules:\n- keep the summary concise\n- make it easy for a business user to understand\n- do not use overly technical wording\n- do not omit the quantity or UOM details\n\n**IMPORTANT\n**For the Lot column, if the`LotNumber` is not present in the json object keep the value blank (do not fill it with values like N/A, not available,etc)\n**For the Quantity column,display both the `Quantity` and `UOMCode` together, if there is no value for `Quantity` keep the value blank (do not fill it with values like N/A, not available,etc)"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set lot items context variable"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775657990578"
          },
          "code": "SET_LOT_ITEMS_CONTEXT_VARIABLE",
          "id": "1778792054444",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778792067139",
              "name": "LotItems",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "array",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.POPULATE_LOT_ENABLED_ITEMS_ARRAY.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display alternate lots"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_ALTERNATE_LOTS",
          "id": "1775667535233",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775667535235_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use this array of JSON objects to generate exactly one `multiRecordWidget`:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_VIEW_LOTS_DATA.$output.result}}\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nDATA EXTRACTION\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFrom each object in the array, extract these fields for display:\n- `LotNumber`\n- `ActualValue`\n\nAlso extract these fields for configuration and actions:\n- `ParameterCode`\n- `WorkOrderId`\n- `Batch`\n- `ItemNumber`\n- `InventoryItemId`\n- `AllLots`\n\nImportant:\n- `ParameterCode` is used to dynamically generate widget columns\n- `WorkOrderId`, `Batch`, `ItemNumber`, `InventoryItemId`, and `AllLots` are not displayed, but must be used where required below\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nHEADER AND SUMMARY\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDisplay this header before the multiRecordWidget:\n\nAlternate Lots for <ItemNumber>\n\nUse the extracted `ItemNumber` value in the header.\n\nBelow the header, display a short summary explaining that:\n- these are available alternate lots for the selected item\n- the lot options are shown based on the actual values defined for the conformance parameters\n\nKeep the summary brief and user-friendly.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nWIDGET STRUCTURE\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nGenerate exactly one `multiRecordWidget`.\n\nThe widget must include:\n- one column named `Lot`\n- additional dynamic columns based on the unique `ParameterCode` values found in the array\n\nColumn rules:\n- `Lot` column = `LotNumber`\n- each dynamic column title = one unique `ParameterCode`\n- the value shown in each dynamic `ParameterCode` column = the corresponding `ActualValue` for that lot and parameter\n\nImportant:\n- group the data by `LotNumber`\n- each row should represent one lot\n- if multiple records share the same `LotNumber`, place their `ActualValue` values under the appropriate dynamic `ParameterCode` columns in the same row\n- If the actual value is not present for a lot then use the character '-' for the actual value\n- do not create duplicate rows for the same lot unless the data truly represents different lots\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nROW ACTION\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nEach row in the `multiRecordWidget` must include this action:\n\n- `title`: `Select`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\":\"SimulateLots\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>,\"ItemId\":<InventoryItemId>,\"SelectedLot\":<LotNumber>,\"AllLots\":<AllLots>})`\n- `actionText`: `Select`\n- `shortDescription`: `Selects the lot for substitution`\n\nUse the values associated with that row’s lot.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nIMPORTANT RULES\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n- Generate exactly one `multiRecordWidget`\n- Use `LotNumber` for the `Lot` column\n- Dynamically create columns from unique `ParameterCode` values\n- Show `ActualValue` in the matching parameter column for each lot\n- Include the row action on every row\n- Do not display internal-only fields such as `WorkOrderId`, `Batch`, `InventoryItemId`, or `AllLots`\n- Keep the summary concise and clear"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_SCM_MANUFACTUR_TESTINGCONFORMANCE2",
            "functionName": "getLatestSimulationByWorkOrderId",
            "name": "Retrieve lot simulation results"
          },
