          "code": "DISPLAY_ERROR_TABLES",
          "id": "1775846337514",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775846337516_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You have the following JSON object: {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_VIEW_ERRORS_DATA.$output.result}}\n\n1.Extract the values for 'WorkOrderId','Batch','AssignmentErrors','TargetValuesErrors','UomConversionErrors' and 'QtyNotReservedErrors' from the JSON fields.\n\n2. As you can see, the fields for 'AssignmentErrors','TargetValuesErrors','UomConversionErrors' and 'QtyNotReservedErrors' contain arrays of JSON objects (each field contains its own array), I want you yo extract the field <ErrorMessage> from each JSON object in the array and create a multiRecordWidget for  'AssignmentErrors','TargetValuesErrors','UomConversionErrors' and 'QtyNotReservedErrors'.\n\nDisplay a brief summary BEFORE all the headers mentioning that there are the errors found during conformance check for the batch <Batch> (where Batch is the value you extracted) , invite the user to check the conformance parameters setup to solve these issues.\n\n3.The columns for each multiRecordWidget should be \"Error\", populate each row in the multiRecordWidget with the value <ErrorMessage> that you extracted for each item.\n\n**IMPORTANT**\nNever show the value for \"WorkOrderId\" , only mention the <Batch> (value you extracted from the array)\nDo NOT display the multirecordwidget if there are no values for certain error groups\nOnly show the widgets that have rows (errors) in them.\nThe header for the AssignmentErrors widget should be \"Conformance parameter assignment errors\"\nThe header for the TargetValuesErrorswidget should be \"Target values errors\"\nThe header for the UomConversionErrors widget should be \"Uom conversion errors\"\nThe header for the QtyNotReservedErrors widget should be \"Ingredients have not been reserved\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create view recommendation data",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "let data = $context.$nodes.GET_RECOMMENDATION_RESULTS.$output.items;\nlet jsonArr = [];\ndata.forEach( item => {\n    let ingredients = item.ConformanceCheckIngredientDetails.items;\n    ingredients.forEach( ingredient => {\n      if(ingredient.RecommendationPriority){\n           if(ingredient.RecommendationPriority === \"1\") {\n        jsonArr.push( {\n          \"Ingredient\": ingredient.ItemNumber,\n          \"ConformanceParameter\": item.ParameterCode,\n          \"Lot\": ingredient.LotNumber,\n          \"SubstituteIngredient\": ingredient.SubstituteInventoryItemNumber,\n          \"SubstituteLot\": ingredient.SubstituteLotNumber,\n          \"ConformanceParameter\": item.ParameterCode,\n          \"OriginalActualValue\": ingredient.IngredientActualValue,\n          \"RecommendationActualValue\": ingredient.ActualValue,\n          \"OriginalQuantity\": ingredient.Quantity,\n          \"OriginalUOM\": ingredient.UOMCodeMeaning,\n          \"RecommendationQuantity\": ingredient.IngredientOnhandQuantity,\n          \"RecommendationUOM\": ingredient.UOMCodeOnhandQuantityMeaning\n        });\n      }\n      }\n      \n    });\n  \n});\nreturn jsonArr;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778603369523"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_VIEW_RECOMMENDATION_DATA",
          "id": "1778531944335",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Below the widget, display the 3 extra actions mentioned"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display user message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_USER_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1774472357760",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774472357761_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the JSON array below to generate exactly one `multiRecordWidget`:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_RUN_CHECK_VIEW_INGREDIENTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result}}\n\nAlso use this conformance check summary input:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_RUN_CHECK_ATTRIBUTES.$output.result}}\n\nYour output must include, in this order:\n\n1. A header\n2. A brief summary\n3. One `multiRecordWidget`\n4. Extra actions displayed below the widget\n\n-----------------------------------\nDATA EXTRACTION RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\nFrom each object in the JSON array, extract these fields for the widget rows:\n\n- `ParameterCode`\n- `MinimumTargetValue`\n- `MaximumTargetValue`\n- `TargetValue`\n- `CalculatedValue`\n- `ConformanceCheckResultStatus`\n\nAlso extract these supporting fields as needed for actions, header content, and summary content:\n\n- `ParentHash`\n- `DetailId`\n- `WorkOrderId`\n- `Batch`\n- `PrimaryProduct`\n- `BatchQuantity`\n- `UomCode`\n- `UOMCodeConformanceParameter`\n- `QuantityConformanceParameter`\n- `OverallStatus`\n- `ConformanceCheckDate`\n\nUse only values extracted from the provided inputs.\n\nDo not display `WorkOrderId` to the user anywhere in the response.\n\nIf you need to refer to the batch in user-facing text, use `Batch` or WorkOrderNumber if available, but never `WorkOrderId`.\n\n-----------------------------------\nOVERALL STATUS RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\nDetermine the overall status from the conformance results in the data.\n\nUse this priority when multiple statuses are present:\n\n1. If any row is `Incomplete`, overall status = `INCOMPLETE`\n2. Else if any row is `Out of range`, overall status = `OUT_OF_RANGE`\n3. Else overall status = `In range`\n\nUse this calculated overall status for the header, summary, and conditional extra actions.\n\n-----------------------------------\nMULTIRECORDWIDGET HEADER RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\nBuild the header using one of the following exact formats:\n\nIf overall status is `In range`, display:\n\n`<PrimaryProduct> (<BatchQuantity> <UomCode>) is in conformance`\n\nIf overall status is `Out of range`, display:\n\n`<PrimaryProduct> (<BatchQuantity> <UomCode>) is out of conformance`\n\nIf overall status is `Incomplete`, display:\n\n`<PrimaryProduct> (<BatchQuantity> <UomCode>) has incomplete results`\n\nHeader requirements:\n\n- Use the extracted values exactly as provided.\n- Do not add extra punctuation.\n- Do not add text before or after the header.\n- Use only one of the three header formats above.\n\n-----------------------------------\nSUMMARY RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\nBelow the header, provide a brief summary of the conformance check using:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_RUN_CHECK_ATTRIBUTES.$output.result}}\n\nThe summary must:\n\n- Mention the execution date in `MM/DD/YYYY` format using `ConformanceCheckDate`\n- Mention the overall conformance check status\n- Provide useful context for the user about the batch result\n- Be concise but informative\n- Avoid exposing technical IDs\n\nIf the overall status is `Incomplete` or `Out of range`, include a helpful hint telling the user to review:\n\n- the conformance parameter setup\n- the actual values\n- the ingredients used in the batch\n- quantites used in the ingredients\n- possible substitutes to be used \n\n-----------------------------------\nMULTIRECORDWIDGET REQUIREMENTS\n-----------------------------------\n\nGenerate exactly one `multiRecordWidget`.\n\nThe widget columns must be exactly:\n\n- `Conformance Parameter`\n- `Minimum Value`\n- `Maximum Value`\n- `Target Value`\n- `Calculated Value`\n- `Conformance Result`\n\nPopulate each row as follows:\n\n- `Conformance Parameter` = `ParameterCode`\n- `Minimum Value` = `MinimumTargetValue`\n- `Maximum Value` = `MaximumTargetValue`\n- `Target Value` = `TargetValue`\n- `Calculated Value` = `CalculatedValue`\n- `Conformance Result` = `ConformanceCheckResultStatus`\n\n-----------------------------------\nROW-LEVEL ACTION RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\nEach row in the `multiRecordWidget` must include exactly one row-level action.\n\nIf `ConformanceCheckResultStatus` is `In range` or `Out of range`, use this action:\n\n- `title`: `\"ViewIngredients\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\": \"ViewIngredients\",\"HashId\": <ParentHash>,\"DetailId\": <DetailId>,\"ParameterCode\": <ParameterCode>,\"ProductQuantity\": <QuantityConformanceParameter>,\"UomCode\": <UOMCodeConformanceParameter>})`\n- `actionText`: `\"View Ingredients\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"View the ingredients related to this conformance parameter\"`\n\nIf `ConformanceCheckResultStatus` is `Incomplete`, use this action:\n\n- `title`: `\"ViewErrors\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\": \"ViewErrors\",\"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\": <Batch>})`\n- `actionText`: `\"View Errors\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"View the conformance check errors for the specified batch\"`\n\nImportant row action rules:\n\n- Always include the appropriate action for each row.\n- For rows with `In range` or `Out of range`, use `ViewIngredients`.\n- For rows with `Incomplete`, use `ViewErrors`.\n- Use values from the same row when building the row-level action.\n\n-----------------------------------\nEXTRA ACTIONS BELOW THE WIDGET\n-----------------------------------\n\nDisplay extra actions below the `multiRecordWidget`.\n\nThe `View Recommendations` action is conditional.\n\nDisplay `View Recommendations` only when the calculated overall status is `Out of range`.\n\nDo not display `View Recommendations` when the calculated overall status is `In range` or `Incomplete`.\n\nAction 1: View Recommendations\n\nDisplay this action only when calculated overall status = `Out of range`.\n\n- `title`: `\"View Recommendations\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\": \"ViewRecommendation\",\"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\": <Batch>})`\n- `actionText`: `\"View Recommendations\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"View the recommended ingredients to fix conformance issues\"`\n\nAlways display the following three actions below the widget, regardless of overall status:\n\nAction 2: Recalculate for alternate ingredient lots\n\n- `title`: `\"Recalculate for alternate ingredient lots\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\": \"SimulateLots\",\"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\": <Batch>})`\n- `actionText`: `\"Recalculate for alternate ingredient lots\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"Simulate the conformance check with substitute lots\"`\n\nAction 3: Recalculate for substitute ingredient\n\n- `title`: `\"Recalculate for substitute ingredient\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\": \"SimulateIngredients\",\"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\": <Batch>,\"HashId\": <ParentHash>,\"DetailId\": <DetailId>})`\n- `actionText`: `\"Recalculate for substitute ingredient\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"Simulate the conformance check with substitute ingredients\"`\n\nAction 4: Recalculate for adjusted quantities\n\n- `title`: `\"Recalculate for adjusted quantities\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\": \"SimulateQuantities\",\"WorkOrderId\": <WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\": <Batch>})`\n- `actionText`: `\"Recalculate for adjusted quantities\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"Simulate the conformance check with adjusted quantities\"`\n\n-----------------------------------\nIMPORTANT OUTPUT RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\n- Generate exactly one `multiRecordWidget`.\n- Always display the header, summary, and widget.\n- Always display the three recalculation actions below the widget.\n- Display `View Recommendations` only when the calculated overall status is `Out of range`.\n- Do not display `View Recommendations` for `In range` or `Icnomplete` results.\n- Never display `WorkOrderId` in user-facing text.\n- Do not omit any row actions.\n- If status is `Incomplete` or `Out of range`, include guidance to review parameter setup, actual values, and ingredients.\n- Keep the wording user-friendly and concise.\n- Use only the extracted values from the provided inputs."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Construct alternate lots data",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "let itemsData = $context.$variables.LotItems;\nlet allLots= $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.AllLots;\n\n// New array to store JSON objects\nlet result = [];\nlet allLotsString = \"[EMPTY]\";\n\n\nif(allLots===\"[EMPTY]\"){\n            if ($context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.ItemId!==null){\n\n                if($context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.ItemId!==\"\"){\n                    let inventoryItemId= $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.ItemId;\n                    let lotN = $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.SelectedLot;\n\n                    if(inventoryItemId){\n                        if(inventoryItemId.toString().trim() !== \"\"){\n                            inventoryItemId = inventoryItemId;\n                        }else{\n                            inventoryItemId = \"[NOT_SET]\";\n                        }\n                    }else{\n                        inventoryItemId = \"[NOT_SET]\";\n                    }\n\n                    if(lotN){\n                        if(lotN.toString().trim() !== \"\"){\n                            lotN = lotN;\n                        }else{\n                            lotN = \"[NOT_SET]\";\n                        }\n                    }else{\n                        lotN = \"[NOT_SET]\";\n                    }\n\n                    let entry = inventoryItemId  + \"<AUX>\" + lotN;\n                    allLotsString = entry;\n\n                }\n            }\n\n }else{\n           if ($context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.ItemId!==null){\n\n                if($context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.ItemId!==\"\"){\n                    \n                    let inventoryItemId= $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.ItemId;\n                    let lotN = $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.SelectedLot;\n\n                    if(inventoryItemId){\n                        if(inventoryItemId.toString().trim() !== \"\"){\n                            inventoryItemId = inventoryItemId;\n                        }else{\n                            inventoryItemId = \"[NOT_SET]\";\n                        }\n                    }else{\n                        inventoryItemId = \"[NOT_SET]\";\n                    }\n\n                    if(lotN){\n                        if(lotN.toString().trim() !== \"\"){\n                            lotN = lotN;\n                        }else{\n                            lotN = \"[NOT_SET]\";\n                        }\n                    }else{\n                        lotN = \"[NOT_SET]\";\n                    }\n\n                    let entry = inventoryItemId  + \"<AUX>\" + lotN ;\n                    allLots = allLots+\"<LOT_SEPARATOR>\"+entry;\n                    allLotsString = allLots;\n\n\n                    let lotMap = {};\n                    let allLotsStringArr = allLotsString .split(\"<LOT_SEPARATOR>\");\n\n                    allLotsStringArr.forEach(lot => {\n                            \n                            if (!lot) return; // skip empty entries\n\n                            let lotCombo = lot.split(\"<AUX>\");\n\n                            let itemId = lotCombo[0];\n                            let selectedLot = lotCombo[1];\n\n                            if (itemId) {\n                                if(selectedLot){\n                                    lotMap [itemId] = selectedLot;\n                                }\n                            }\n                     });\n\n                }                    \n            }\n}\n\n\nlet allLotsMap = {};\n\nif (allLotsString) {\n\n    if(allLotsString !==\"[EMPTY]\"){\n        let allLotsStringArr = allLotsString .split(\"<LOT_SEPARATOR>\");\n\n        allLotsStringArr.forEach(lot => {\n            if (!lot) return; // skip empty entries\n\n            let lotCombo = lot.split(\"<AUX>\");\n\n            let itemId = lotCombo[0];\n            let selectedLot = lotCombo[1];\n\n            if (itemId) {\n                if(selectedLot){\n                    allLotsMap[itemId] = selectedLot;\n                }\n            }\n        });\n    }\n}\n\nif(allLotsString){\n    if(allLotsString .toString().trim() !== \"[EMPTY]\" || allLotsString .toString().trim() !== \"\" ){\n        allLotsString=allLotsString;\n    }else{\n        allLotsString = \"[EMPTY]\";\n    }\n}else{\n    allLotsString = \"[EMPTY]\";\n}\n\n\nif(itemsData!=null){\n    if(itemsData.length!==0){\n        itemsData.forEach((item, index) => {\n            \n        let obj = {\n            \"WorkOrderId\": $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.WorkOrderId,\n            \"Batch\": $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SIMULATE_LOTS_PAYLOAD.$output.result.Batch,\n            \"ItemNumber\": item.ItemNumber,\n            \"InventoryItemId\":item.InventoryItemId,\n            \"OriginalLot\":item.OriginalLot,\n            \"SelectedLot\": allLotsMap[item.InventoryItemId],\n            \"AllLots\": allLotsString\n        };\n\n            result.push(obj);\n        });\n\n    }\n     \n}\n\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775685080125"
          },
          "code": "CONSTRUCT_ALTERNATE_LOTS_DATA",
          "id": "1775657990578",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract lot simulation results",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "let data = $context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_LOT_SIMULATION_RESULTS.$output.items;\n\nlet jsonArr = [];\n\nfor (const detail of data) {\n   let newObj = {\n      \"ParameterCode\":detail.ParameterCode,\n      \"MinimumTargetValue\":detail.MinimumTargetValue,\n      \"MaximumTargetValue\":detail.MaximumTargetValue,\n      \"TargetValue\":detail.TargetValue,\n      \"CalculatedValue\":detail.CalculatedValue,\n      \"ConformanceCheckResultStatus\":detail.ConformanceCheckResultStatus,\n      \"Batch\":detail.WorkOrderNumber,\n      \"WorkOrderId\":detail.WorkOrderId,\n      \"ConformanceCheckResultDate\":detail.ConformanceCheckResultDate\n   };\n\n  jsonArr.push(newObj);\n}\n\nreturn jsonArr;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775690807657"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_LOT_SIMULATION_RESULTS",
          "id": "1777311940903",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create view recommendation general results",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "let data = $context.$nodes.GET_RECOMMENDATION_RESULTS.$output.items;\n\nlet results = [];\n\ndata.forEach(item=>{\n\n       const status= item.ConformanceCheckResultStatus.replaceAll(\"_\", \" \");\n       let newItem = {\n             \"ConformanceParameter\":item.ParameterCode,\n             \"SimulatedValue\":item.CalculatedValue,\n             \"ConformanceStatus\":status,\n             \"WorkOrderId\":item.WorkOrderId,\n             \"Batch\":item.WorkOrderNumber\n       };\n\n       results.push(newItem);\n});\n\nreturn results;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778534141117"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_VIEW_RECOMMENDATION_GENERAL_RESULTS",
          "id": "1778603369523",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Construct simulation parameters",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let itemsData = $context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_ALTERNATE_LOTS_DATA.$output.result;\n\nlet parametersString = null;\n\n\nitemsData .forEach((item, index) => {\n        if(index===0){\n               parametersString = item.ItemNumber + \"||\"+ item.OriginalLot + \"||\" + item.SelectedLot;\n        }else{\n              parametersString = parametersString + \"<LOT_SIMULATION>\" +  item.ItemNumber + \"||\"+ item.OriginalLot + \"||\" + item.SelectedLot;\n        }\n});\n\nreturn parametersString;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775658645705"
          },
          "code": "CONSTRUCT_SIMULATION_PARAMETERS",
          "id": "1775685080125",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
