          "code": "DISPLAY_LOT_SIMULATION_RESULTS",
          "id": "1775690807657",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775690807659_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following  array of Json object to generate a single multiRecordWidget : {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_LOT_SIMULATION_RESULTS.$output.result}}\n\nThe columns for the multiRecordWidget should be \"Conformance Parameter\",\"Minimum Value\",\"Maximum Value\",\"Target Value\",\"Calculated Value\" and \"Conformance Result\"\n\n1) Extract `ParameterCode`, `MinimumTargetValue`,`MaximumTargetValue`,`TargetValue`,`CalculatedValue`,`ConformanceCheckResultStatus`  from each JSON inside the array to populate the rows in the multiRecordWidget \n**Also extract  `WorkOrderId` and `Batch`\n\nDisplay the header:\n\nConformance check simulation results\n\nThen write a brief, user-friendly summary of the simulation results for the batch <Batch> (where <Batch> is the value you extracted )\n\nThe summary must:\n- mention the simulation execution date in `MM/DD/YYYY` format\n- mention the overall conformance check simulation status\n- highlight the most useful result for the user\n- clearly state that these are simulation-only results\n- clearly state that the batch itself has not been changed yet\n- tell the user that they still need to apply or make the desired changes to the batch if they want those changes reflected in the actual batch\n\nUse a clear and concise tone.\nDo not describe the simulation as an actual batch update.\nDo not imply that the batch was changed automatically.\n\n**IMPORTANT\n**Do not mention the WorkOrderId, only WorkOrderNumber/Batch\n**If the status is either \"INCOMPLETE\" or \"OUT_OF_RANGE\" you should give a hint to the user of reviewing the conformance parameter setup, the actual values and the ingredients of the batch."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
