          "code": "DISPLAY_VIEW_RECOMMENDATIONS",
          "id": "1778534141117",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778534141118_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following JSON array to generate one `multiRecordWidget` section:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_VIEW_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nThe output using  this json array should be:\n\n1. A header\n2. A brief summary exaplaining that the ingredients shown were selected as they are out of range and they have a high contribution to the overall result\n3. One `multiRecordWidget` with row-level actions\n\n-----------------------------------\nPRIMARY INPUT STRUCTURE\n-----------------------------------\n\nEach object in the first JSON array contain:\n\n- `ConformanceParameter`\n- `Ingredient`\n- `Lot`\n- `SubstituteIngredient`\n- `SubstituteLot`\n\nEach object also include these additional fields for row-level actions only:\n\n- `OriginalActualValue`\n- `RecommendationActualValue`\n- `OriginalQuantity`\n- `RecommendationQuantity`\n- `RecommendationUOM`\n- `OriginalUOM`\n\nDo not display the action-only fields as widget columns.\n\n-----------------------------------\nRECOMMENDATION WIDGET RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\nThe recommendation widget columns must be exactly:\n\n- `Conformance Parameter`\n- `Ingredient`\n- `Lot`\n- `Substitute`\n- `Alternate Lot`\n\nPopulate each recommendation widget row as follows using the array of json objects:\n\n- `Ingredient` = value of `Ingredient`\n- `Lot` = value of `Lot`\n- `Substitute` = value of `SubstituteIngredient`\n- `Alternate Lot` = value of `SubstituteLot`\n\nDo not add, remove, rename, or reorder these columns.\n\n-----------------------------------\nROW-LEVEL ACTION RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\nEvery row in the `multiRecordWidget` must include a row-level `Details` action.\n\nThe row action must use values from the same object used to populate that row.\n\nFor each row, generate this action:\n\n- `title`: `\"Details\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\":\"ViewRecommendationDetails\",\"ingredient\":<Ingredient>,\"lot\":<Lot>,\"substituteIngredient\":<SubstituteIngredient>,\"alternateLot\":<SubstituteLot>,\"conformanceParameter\":<ConformanceParameter>,\"originalActualValue\":<OriginalActualValue>,\"recommendationActualValue\":<RecommendationActualValue>,\"originalQuantity\":<OriginalQuantity>,\"recommendationQuantity\":<RecommendationQuantity>,\"recommendationUOM\":<RecommendationUOM>,\"originalUOM\":<OriginalUOM>})`\n- `actionText`: `\"Details\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"View the recommendation details\"`\n\nField mapping for the row action:\n\n- `<Ingredient>` = value of `Ingredient`\n- `<Lot>` = value of `Lot`\n- `<SubstituteIngredient>` = value of `SubstituteIngredient`\n- `<SubstituteLot>` = value of `SubstituteLot`\n- `<ConformanceParameter>` = value of `ConformanceParameter`\n- `<OriginalActualValue>` = value of `OriginalActualValue`\n- `<RecommendationActualValue>` = value of `RecommendationActualValue`\n- `<OriginalQuantity>` = value of `OriginalQuantity`\n- `<RecommendationQuantity>` = value of `RecommendationQuantity`\n\nDo not omit row actions for any recommendation row.\n\n-----------------------------------\nFINAL CONFORMANCE RESULTS WIDGET\n-----------------------------------\n\nAfter generating the first widget, generate exactly one final `multiRecordWidget` using the following JSON array:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_VIEW_RECOMMENDATION_GENERAL_RESULTS.$output.result}}\n\nThis final widget must include:\n\n1. A header\n2. A brief summary explaining the simulated conformance check results after using the recommended substitute ingredients/lots \n3. One `multiRecordWidget` populated from the general results array\n\nThe final widget columns must be exactly:\n\n- `Conformance Parameter`\n- `Simulated Value`\n- `Conformance Status`\n\nPopulate each final widget row as follows:\n\n- `Conformance Parameter` = value of `ConformanceParameter`\n- `Simulated Value` = value of `SimulatedValue`\n- `Conformance Status` = value of `ConformanceStatus` (display a badge with dependning on the Status,if its in rage use priority: success , otherwise use priority:alert)\n\nDo not add, remove, rename, or reorder these final widget columns.\n\n-----------------------------------\nFINAL ACTIONS AFTER ALL WIDGETS\n-----------------------------------\n\nAfter all widgets are displayed, generate exactly three final actions.\n\nUse this JSON array to extract shared action values:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_VIEW_RECOMMENDATION_GENERAL_RESULTS.$output.result}}\n\nExtract the following values from the general results array:\n\n- `WorkOrderId`\n- `Batch`\n\nThese values are expected to be the same across all items in the array. Use the first available non-null value for each.\n\nGenerate the following three actions exactly:\n\n1. Recalculate for alternate ingredient lots\n\n- `title`: `\"Recalculate for alternate ingredient lots\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\":\"SimulateLots\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>})`\n- `actionText`: `\"Recalculate for alternate ingredient lots\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"Simulate conformance check with substitute lots\"`\n\n2. Recalculate for substitute ingredient\n\n- `title`: `\"Recalculate for substitute ingredient\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\":\"SimulateIngredients\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>,\"HashId\":1,\"DetailId\":1})`\n- `actionText`: `\"Recalculate for substitute ingredient\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"Simulate conformance check with substitute ingredients\"`\n\n3. Recalculate for adjusted quantities\n\n- `title`: `\"Recalculate for adjusted quantities\"`\n- `followUpCommand`: `ora.Agent({\"command\":\"SimulateQuantities\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>})`\n- `actionText`: `\"Recalculate for adjusted quantities\"`\n- `shortDescription`: `\"Simulate conformance check with substitute quantities\"`\n\n-----------------------------------\nIMPORTANT OUTPUT RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\n- Generate exactly one recommendation `multiRecordWidget` for the first JSON array.\n- Generate exactly one final conformance results `multiRecordWidget` after the first widget.\n- Generate exactly three final actions after all widgets.\n- Always include a header, brief summary, and widget for every widget section.\n- Always include the specified `Details` row action for the first widget.\n- Use the final JSON array only to populate the final conformance results widget and extract `WorkOrderId` and `Batch` for final actions.\n- Use only values extracted from the provided JSON inputs.\n- Do not invent missing values.\n- If a displayed value is missing or null, leave the corresponding widget cell blank.\n- If an action value is missing or null, pass an empty string for that action parameter.\n- Keep all wording concise, clear, and user-friendly.\n- Do not omit any item from either JSON array.\n- Do not add extra widgets, columns, rows, or actions beyond what is requested.\n- Never mention any internal IDs you see\n- Never mention the word widget to the user"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Display the Recalculate conformance action below the widget"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display selected alteranate lots"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_SELECTED_ALTERANATE_LOTS",
          "id": "1775658645705",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775658645708_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following  array of Json object to generate a single multiRecordWidget : {{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_ALTERNATE_LOTS_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nThe columns for the multiRecordWidget should be \"Ingredient\",\"Original Lot\",\"Alternate Lot\"\n\nDisplay a header with title \"Alternate Lots\" if there are items in the array, if no items are available, display \"Lot ingredients not found\"\nAlso display a small summary saying that these are the Lot enabled ingredients and that user can select alternate lots using the action specified.\n\n1) Extract `ItemNumber`, `OriginalLot`,`SelectedLot`  from each JSON inside the array to populate the rows in the multiRecordWidget \n**Also extract `InventoryItemId`,`WorkOrderId` ,`Batch`, `AllLots` from each JSON, this will not be shown but will be used below**\n\n** For each row in the multiRecordWidget , generate an actionable insight using the following options:\ntitle:\"ViewLots\"\nfollowUpCommand: ora.Agent({\"command\": \"ViewLots\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>,\"InventoryItemId\":<InventoryItemId>,\"AllLots\":<AllLots>})   where <WorkOrderId>,<Batch> ,<InventoryItemId> and <AllLots> are the values you extracted from the array \nactionText: \"View Lots\"\nshortDescription: \"Views the alternate lots for the selected ingredient\"\n\nAdditionally, below the multiRecordWidget, display another actionable insight with the following properties:\ntitle:\"Recalculate Conformance check\"\nfollowUpCommand: ora.Agent({\"command\": \"SubmitLotSimulation\",\"WorkOrderId\":<WorkOrderId>,\"Batch\":<Batch>,\"SimulationParameters\":<{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_SIMULATION_PARAMETERS.$output.result}}>\"})   where <WorkOrderId>,<Batch>  are the values you extracted from the array \nactionText: \"Recalculate Conformance check\"\nshortDescription: \"Recalculates the conformance check with the substitute lots\"\n\n**Important**\n*Display N/A for Alternate Lots column if the value is not available.\n*Each row in the multiRecordWidget should have  its own 'View Lots' action\n*The 'View Lots' action should only be displayed in each row.\n*Do not forget to display the Recalculate conformance action below the widget\n*Do not add extra characters or escape characters in the commands specified (backslash or things like that)"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract apply recommendation payload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const payload = $context.$nodes.CREATE_ACTION_OBJECT.$output.result;\n\nconst obj = {\n     \"WorkOrderId\":Number(payload.WorkOrderId),\n     \"Batch\":payload.Batch\n};\n\nreturn obj;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780346627287"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_APPLY_RECOMMENDATION_PAYLOAD",
          "id": "1779306634408",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ]
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display results after applying recommendation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_RESULTS_AFTER_APPLYING_RECOMMENDATION",
          "id": "1779307368939",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779307368939_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1779307368939_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use the following JSON array to generate one `multiRecordWidget` section:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_POST_RECOMMENDATION_INGREDIENTS_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nThe output using  this json array should be:\n\n1. A header with the title 'Batch ingredients and quantities'\n2. A brief summary explaining that after applying the recommendation provided by the system, the batch is now in conformance.\n3. One `multiRecordWidget`\n\n-----------------------------------\nPRIMARY INPUT STRUCTURE\n-----------------------------------\n\nEach object in the first JSON array contain:\n\n- `Ingredient`\n- `Lot`\n- `ReservedQuantity`\n\n-----------------------------------\nINGREDIENT WIDGET RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\nThe recommendation widget columns must be exactly:\n\n- `Ingredient`\n- `Lot`\n- `Reserved Quantity`\n\nPopulate each recommendation widget row as follows using the array of json objects:\n\n- `Ingredient` = value of `Ingredient`\n- `Lot` = value of `Lot`\n- `Reserved Quantity` = value of `ReservedQuantity`\n\nDo not add, remove, rename, or reorder these columns.\n\n-----------------------------------\nFINAL CONFORMANCE RESULTS WIDGET\n-----------------------------------\n\nAfter generating the first widget, generate exactly one final `multiRecordWidget` using the following JSON array:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_POST_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nThis final widget must include:\n\n1. A header with the title 'Conformance Results'\n2. A brief summary explaining the conformance check results after using the recommended substitute ingredients/lots \n3. One `multiRecordWidget` populated from the general results array\n\nThe final widget columns must be exactly:\n\n- `Conformance Parameter`\n- `Minimum Value`\n- `Maximum Value`\n- `Target Value`\n- `Calculated Value`\n- `Conformance Result`\n\nPopulate each final widget row as follows:\n\n- `Conformance Parameter` = value of `ConformanceParameter`\n- `Minimum Value` = value of `MinumumValue`\n- `Maximum Value` = value of `MaximumValue`\n- `Target Value` = value of `TargetValue`\n- `Calculated Value` = value of `CalculatedValue`\n- `Conformance Result` = value of `ConformanceCheckStatus` (display a badge with depending on the Status,if its in rage use priority: success , otherwise use priority:alert)\n\nDo not add, remove, rename, or reorder these final widget columns.\n\n-----------------------------------\nIMPORTANT OUTPUT RULES\n-----------------------------------\n\n- Generate exactly one recommendation `multiRecordWidget` for the first JSON array.\n- Generate exactly one final conformance results `multiRecordWidget` after the first widget.\n- Always include a header, brief summary, and widget for every widget section.\n- Use only values extracted from the provided JSON inputs.\n- Do not invent missing values.\n- If a displayed value is missing or null, leave the corresponding widget cell blank.\n- If an action value is missing or null, pass an empty string for that action parameter.\n- Keep all wording concise, clear, and user-friendly.\n- Do not omit any item from either JSON array.\n- Do not add extra widgets, columns, rows, or actions beyond what is requested.\n- Never mention any internal IDs you see\n- Never mention the word widget to the user"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
